  "caveats": [
    "All seven Java suites run in one fresh isolated build; Python validators were added afterward and are bound separately to their complete normal/optimized suites and exact retained replays.",
    "Six actual public-bootstrap histories cover stable 3/4/5 voters with EMPTY/backup, original BARRIER and DATA publication, native reopen, real TCP activation and a further same-JVM native reopen. No caller historical verifier enters the new production constructors.",
    "The native path requires complete original-owner source transfer and the same exact PREPARE/PROMISE/root/view/ballot/source checks. It creates no new historical voter observation.",
    "Every original history, actual core application image, new grant, fixed quorum, selected installation and reopen is independently reconstructed before intended evidence mutations. Normal, optimized and relocated replay agree.",
    "Boundary tests cover old-history rejection without provenance, correlation, original grants, close/expiry/fencing, unrelated completed pulls, and accepted-tail precedence; existing driver/endpoint/selection fault suites and their evidence are replayed separately.",
    "The first integration probe failed only because the evidence serializer rejected hyphenated object keys; its source snapshot and log are retained. The corrected one-profile build is not substituted for the final six-profile qualification.",
    "The six histories have equal published cuts and explicitly invoked campaigns. Automatic missing-ancestry discovery, unequal compacted cuts, autonomous adoption/elections, cross-view pending contexts, learner/joint transitions, distributed publication and full Phase 3 remain open.",
    "No public factory, durable format, resource/deadline limit, POM, workflow, V5.2 Runner, push, cloud or release change."
  ],
